      "side": 1,
      "message": "If this host vmexit happens while pKVM is still setting up uret msrs in `pkvm_x86_vendor_init()` -\u003e `vmx_hardware_setup()` -\u003e `vmx_setup_user_return_msrs()`, we have a race: pKVM is modifying `kvm_uret_msrs_list` and `kvm_nr_uret_msrs` values on another CPU while using them on this CPU?\n\nWell, we know this will not happen, since the host is not really expected to write these MSRs after deprivileging, except that single case in `vmx_init()` -\u003e `kvm_x86_vendor_init()` -\u003e `vmx_hardware_setup()` -\u003e `vmx_setup_user_return_msrs()` -\u003e `kvm_add_user_return_msr()` -\u003e `kvm_probe_user_return_msr()` which happens after pKVM initialization, not in parallel with it (and the host is still trusted at this point, so we can assume it will indeed not write these MSRs in parallel with pKVM initialization).\n\nBut if we need to make such assumptions anyway, it feels that adding this fragile logic here is not worth it, and we\u0027d better just prevent that single case of writing these MSRs by host after deprivileging, since IIUC that is useless anyway (since IIUC with pKVM enabled, the host itself doesn\u0027t deal with uret MSRs, so it doesn\u0027t need to set them up):\n\n```\n--- a/arch/x86/kvm/vmx/vmx.c\n+++ b/arch/x86/kvm/vmx/vmx.c\n@@ -9368,7 +9368,8 @@ __init int vmx_hardware_setup(void)\n \tstore_idt(\u0026dt);\n \thost_idt_base \u003d dt.address;\n \n-\tvmx_setup_user_return_msrs();\n+\tif (!enable_pkvm)\n+\t\tvmx_setup_user_return_msrs();\n \n \n \tif (boot_cpu_has(X86_FEATURE_NX))\n```\n\nand then just unconditionally inject #GP here and keep it simple?",
      "revId": "a33471f42130f67e0c257bf91646f854a31aec54",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
